"The equation above is the groundwater balance. TWSA is total water storage anomaly; SMSA is soil moisture storage anomaly; SWSA is surface water storage anomaly; CWSA is canopy water storage anomaly; and SWEA is snow water equivalent anomaly. An anomaly is a difference from a reference-period average. Each term must therefore use the same reference before subtraction. Snow is small in Thailand, but its term is retained for a consistent balance.",
"GRACE measures changes in water mass over large areas. It does not measure groundwater separately. The groundwater result depends on both GRACE and the products used to remove the other compartments. A negative GWSA means less groundwater storage than the reference average; it is not the total volume of groundwater left in an aquifer.",
"The main outputs are monthly basin time series, maps of trends and significance, climate-model test scores, residual series and independent observation comparisons. Every map is read together with the corresponding time series and coverage information. Missing data remain missing throughout the analysis."
