"Step 2 applies the groundwater balance on the common valid footprint. The primary calculation uses CSR RL06.3 total storage, GLDAS soil moisture, canopy water and snow, and G3P surface water. The code applies the documented CSR unit conversion and special month assignments. Comparisons with alternative processing chains use their common dates, so a change in record length does not become a product difference.",
"Step 3 estimates change using the seasonal Sen slope. This is a robust summary of the rate of change, expressed in mm/year. A negative slope indicates decline. The seasonal Mann–Kendall test checks for a consistent trend while accounting for the calendar-month pattern. The original Mann–Kendall result is also retained in the output tables.",
"Because many basins are tested, false discovery rate adjustment is applied to the basin tests. Maps distinguish trend size from statistical evidence. A low adjusted p-value does not remove uncertainty in the storage products or make neighbouring basins independent. GRACE has broad spatial support, so a detailed basin outline does not imply equally detailed gravity information."
